{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/388156-professional-training-and-embeds-and-exploits","id":388156,"title":"Professional Training and Embeds and Exploits","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-01T02:12:24-08:00","id":388156,"title":"Professional Training and Embeds and Exploits","content":"So after looking at the verdict of writers regarding Professional Training and the Vampiric Disciplines, I am curious on whether or not such a ruling should apply to Embeds and Exploits. For Exploits, I could understand why things like 9 again and rote might be a bit too much for things which are already breaking the rules of reality, but what about Embeds? Most of these bend rules rather than flat out break them, though, again, I can see why some of them might be a bit game breaking when you factor in PT. Such as Merciless Gunman when the Down and Dirty element of it applies, for example.<br /> <br /> Anyhoo, some developer insight and the thoughts of other players would be greatly appreciated. Thanks in advance!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1353-riche","name":"RichE","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T07:29:26-08:00","id":388391,"title":"","content":"I am of the opinion that the rules, unless specifically stated, no merit applies to the roll of any supernatural power, no matter the game line. So, no Professional Training to add to Embeds, Exploits, Gadgets, or Demon Forms that employ your skills. No to shapeshifting, Gift, or Ritual rolls. No to mage rote or scrutinizing rolls. (the last two under the assumption they will remain the same). I will argue that Professional Training (occult) won't add to Supernatural merits, like psychokinesis, either. The same for Striking Looks, Trained Observer, and the like adding into social powers or powers that rely on observation.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, am I going to use it during my games? That's another matter entirely. I think that Rote Quality may a bit powerful for any contested abilities, especially if you stack bonuses. Its one thing to reroll a handful of dice (lets say five dice out of seven) when it costs you a point of willpower (three dice there). That's a net gain of 2 dice. Its another when you can reroll all failed dice on a dice pool approaching 15 - that's 10 dice. Huge difference.<br /> <br /> <br /> Still, I probably would just go for it. You can't add to Clash of Wills or Aura battles. There are ways around raw damage pumping already.<br /> <br /> <br /> To me, I look at it like this. You can use Professional Training with Brawl or Weaponry or Firearms. You can stack it with lots of other magical things. Why should an execution of something purely magical instead of mostly magically enhanced differ? <br /> <br /> Using willpower on an Exploit may seem over powered, but you have to remember something. You need willpower to suppress the compromise check. And, rote quality on an embed, that's often unopposed anyways? What's the point? <br /> <br /> <br /> It may seem excessive, but, in Demon, I can't see it mattering over much. The only situation I really think applies is when dealing directly with angels, and they shrug off most powers as it is already. In Vampire, Majesty and Nightmare are overcome with a Clash of Wills, and Dominate you just, I don't know, don't look into the Lord's eyes. Obfuscate doesn't call for a lot of rolls, and Animalism as well as Auspex doesn't really affect vampires directly, so its a moot point.<br /> <br /> <br /> Powerful? Undoubtedly. Going to break the game? That's open to debate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 02-01-2015, 10:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}